  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 222 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nAn upper level shortwave trough will move northeast out of the\nsouthern plains and across the area on Tuesday and Tuesday \nnight. Clouds will increase across the area with the trough. A \ndrier air mass will remain in place across the area which will \nlimit the overall rain chances, but some sprinkles will be \npossible at times as lift from the trough moves through the \nregion on Tuesday. \n\nThe upper level ridge will build back over the region on\nWednesday with southerly flow returning. The above normal\ntemperatures will continue as highs in the middle 70s to near \n80 are expected Wednesday and Friday as the upper level ridge\nwill be in place over the region. Clouds will start to increase\non Friday, but the warmer air mass will remain in place with \nhighs in the middle to upper 70s expected.\n\nAnother upper level trough will move northeast out of the\nsouthern plains and across the region late this week into next\nweekend. Better moisture return should occur ahead of this\nsystem which will bring rain chances 40-60% to the area. There\nremains difference between the ensemble model members on the \nexact track and timing of the system and how fast the rain moves\nout of the area. It is possible rain chances starts as early as\nlate Friday and chances could linger into Sunday depending on \nthe exact track and timing.",
